s-west, eu-west). payments-api (v5.1.0) shows matching 18% errors downstream of the worker. Action taken: rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0, its last release that was healthy in production. Next: confirm the worker and payments-api recover, then find the root cause in v3.4.0.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-sev2-rollback", "confidence": 0.92}, "confidence": 0.92}, {"t_ms": 583286, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01BWjkish3CFXy8HYo7D69zm", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-sev2-rollback", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 583286, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01BWjkish3CFXy8HYo7D69zm", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 587769, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened the SEV2. The worker has recovered, but payments-api is still failing, so the fix isn't confirmed yet.\n\n- **Rollback:** payments-worker is now on v3.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west. v3.3.0 was its last release that was healthy in production. It's healthy now, with errors down from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, payments-worker) is open and on-call has been paged. My first attempt to create it timed out. Before retrying, I checked and no incident had been created, and the retry used the same request key, so there's no duplicate page.\n- **Still failing:** my check right after the rollback showed payments-api still unhealthy at 18% errors. It may just need a few minutes to catch up, or it may have its own problem in v5.1.0, which was marked degraded. If it hasn't recovered soon, rolling payments-api back to v5.0.0 (its last release that was healthy in production) is the next step. I haven't done that, because you said the worker was the cause.", "e