": null, "text": "I haven't rolled anything back or opened the incident yet. Two payments services fit your description, and I need you to tell me which one you mean before I change production.\n\n| Service | Current version | Error rate | Previous version (healthy in production) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| payments-api | v5.1.0 (marked degraded) | 18% | v5.0.0 |\n| payments-worker | v3.4.0 (marked unhealthy) | 18% | v3.3.0 |\n\nBoth were last released in a version that's now failing, and both are unhealthy in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The deployment history doesn't include times, so I can't tell which one went out this morning. Their error rates are exactly the same, which suggests one may be breaking the other. You asked about one service, and rolling back the wrong one would add risk without fixing anything. No payments incidents are open yet.\n\nWhich should I do?\n1. Roll back **payments-api** to v5.0.0\n2. Roll back **payments-worker** to v3.3.0\n3. Roll back both\n\nOnce you pick, I'll do the rollback and open the SEV2 incident for that service in one step. If you want on-call paged now, I can open the SEV2 right away with both services in the summary.", "type": "text"}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_014JM9Y2rdPjbKQJr3TCyeFC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01JhDJ1Mscc4WWPNkd3BG5y5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker v3.4.0 causing elevated errors; rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "Since this morning's deploy of payments-worker v3.4.0, the worker is unhealthy with an 18% error rate in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). payments-api (v5.1.0) shows matching 18% errors downstream of the worker. Action taken: rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0, its last release that was healthy in production. Next: confirm the worker and payments-api recover, then find the root cause in v3.4.0.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-sev2-rollback", "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01JGudiZpMJLsH8gZB28TtJU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01HVjgYLmmDub8aeeu65QpvY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016CeCmPNSoMAnTSiNAHa4jn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01BWjkish3CFXy8HYo7D69zm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker v3.4.0 causing elevated errors; rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "Since this morning's deploy of payments-worker v3.4.0, the worker is unhealthy with an 18% error rate in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). payments-api (v5.1.0) shows matching 18% errors downstream of the worker. Action taken: rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0, its last release that was healthy in production. Next: confirm the worker and payments-api recover, then find the root cause in v3.4.0.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-sev2-rollback", "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened the SEV2.